# KHELA HOBE — INITIAL TEST ACCOUNT SETUP

Before final testing, create predefined test accounts for PLAYER, ORGANIZER, and ADMIN roles so the application can be tested without manually registering and promoting users.

### 1. Create These Test Accounts

| Role | Name | Email |
|---|---|---|
| PLAYER | Test Player | player@khelahobe.com |
| ORGANIZER | Test Organizer | organizer@khelahobe.com |
| ADMIN | Test Admin | admin@khelahobe.com |

Use a common development-only password configured through environment variables, or generate separate temporary passwords and document them securely.

### 2. Implementation Requirements

1. Inspect the existing authentication, user, role, and database models before implementation.
2. Create an idempotent database seed script that creates these accounts if they do not already exist.
3. Assign roles directly through the database using the existing role-management system.
4. Ensure the ORGANIZER account has an approved organizer status and can access organizer features immediately.
5. Ensure the ADMIN account has full administrative permissions.
6. Ensure the PLAYER account has only normal player permissions.
7. Hash all passwords using the same secure password-hashing mechanism used by the application.
8. Ensure all three accounts can log in through the existing frontend login page.
9. Verify role-based dashboards, protected routes, and backend API permissions for each account.
10. Do not bypass authentication or authorization to make these accounts work.

### 3. Security Restrictions

- Seed accounts must only be created in development or explicitly authorized testing environments.
- Never create these accounts automatically in production.
- Never hardcode plaintext passwords or production credentials in source code.
- Do not expose admin credentials in frontend code or public API responses.
- Do not create a public admin registration endpoint.
- Admin privileges must only be assigned through trusted server-side provisioning.
- Make the seed operation safe to run multiple times without creating duplicate accounts.

### 4. Testing

After creating the accounts:

- Log in as PLAYER and verify player functionality.
- Log in as ORGANIZER and verify organizer functionality.
- Log in as ADMIN and verify admin functionality.
- Attempt unauthorized operations between roles and confirm they are rejected by the backend.
- Verify logout and session isolation when switching accounts.

### 5. Deliverables

Provide:
- Seed script and execution command.
- Test account email addresses and development login credentials.
- Confirmation that all three accounts were created successfully.
- Role and permission verification results.
- Any database migration or configuration changes.

**Important:** This is temporary test infrastructure for initial QA. Do not weaken the production authentication or authorization system.